1. 6-PART TEST SET ARCHITECTURE & SCORING BLUEPRINT (MANDATORY)

Support and organize test sets into exactly 6 structured Set Types (while keeping 100% backward compatibility with any existing legacy sets, including 70-mark Language + Common Paper sets):

1. **Part 1 – Common Paper (40 Questions | 40 Merit Marks)**
   - Fixed subject breakdown (5 sub-sections of 8 questions each):
     - Mathematics: 8 Questions
     - Science: 8 Questions
     - History: 8 Questions
     - Geography: 8 Questions
     - Current Affairs: 8 Questions
   - Scoring: All 40 marks count toward Set Score, Cutoff, and Common Paper Ranking.

2. **Part 2 – Language Paper (30 Questions | Qualifying Only)**
   - Fixed sub-section breakdown:
     - English: 8 Questions
     - Hindi: 22 Questions
   - Scoring & Qualifying Rule:
     - Combined Language Marks >= 9 out of 30 --> PASS (Qualified)
     - Combined Language Marks < 9 out of 30  --> FAIL (Not Qualified)
     - Strictly Qualifying Only: Language marks are NEVER added to any Merit Score or Rank Card.

3. **Part 3 – Maths (40 Questions | 40 Merit Marks)**
   - Subject: 40 Questions from Mathematics.
   - Scoring: All 40 marks count toward Maths Set Score and Maths Ranking.

4. **Part 4 – Science (40 Questions | 40 Merit Marks)**
   - Subject: 40 Questions from Science.
   - Scoring: All 40 marks count toward Science Set Score and Science Ranking.

5. **Part 5 – Full Length Set (Maths & Science) (150 Questions | 120 Merit Marks + 30 Qualifying)**
   - Composition: Combines **Part 1 (Common Paper – 40 Q)** + **Part 2 (Language Paper – 30 Q)** + **Part 3 (Maths – 40 Q)** + **Part 4 (Science – 40 Q)**.
   - Scoring & Rank Rule:
     - Part 2 (Language – 30 Q) is evaluated separately as **Qualifying Only** (Combined >= 9/30 = PASS, < 9/30 = FAIL) and is **EXCLUDED** from Merit Score & Rank Card.
     - Merit Score, Cutoff, Percentile, and Rank are calculated strictly out of **120 Marks** (40 Common Paper + 40 Maths + 40 Science).

6. **Part 6 – Full Length Set (Mathematics) (150 Questions | 120 Merit Marks + 30 Qualifying)**
   - Composition: Combines **Part 1 (Common Paper – 40 Q)** + **Part 2 (Language Paper – 30 Q)** + **Part 3 (Maths – 40 Q)** + **Additional Mathematics Section (40 Q)** (total 80 Mathematics questions).
   - Scoring & Rank Rule:
     - Part 2 (Language – 30 Q) is evaluated separately as **Qualifying Only** (Combined >= 9/30 = PASS, < 9/30 = FAIL) and is **EXCLUDED** from Merit Score & Rank Card.
     - Merit Score, Cutoff, Percentile, and Rank are calculated strictly out of **120 Marks** (40 Common Paper + 80 Mathematics).

Legacy Compatibility Note:
- If any existing 70-mark **"Language + Common Paper"** set (30 Language + 40 Common Paper) exists in the database, enforce the same rule: Language (30) is Qualifying Only (9/30 to pass) and is NEVER added to the 40-mark Common Paper score — Merit & Rank are strictly out of **40 Marks** (NOT 70).

