12. ADVANCED INDEPENDENT RANKING SYSTEM

Calculate ALL rankings exclusively from immutable Original Test Attempts (NEVER use Solution Reattempt records).

A. Independent Set-Wise & Part-Wise Ranking:
- Maintain completely isolated leaderboards for every Set Type and Set Number:
  - **Part 1 (Common Paper – Set 1, Set 2, ...):** Ranked out of 40 Marks.
  - **Part 2 (Language Paper – Set 1, Set 2, ...):** Qualifying Status ONLY (PASS >= 9/30, FAIL < 9/30) — NO Merit Rank.
  - **Part 3 (Maths – Set 1, Set 2, ...):** Ranked out of 40 Marks.
  - **Part 4 (Science – Set 1, Set 2, ...):** Ranked out of 40 Marks.
  - **Part 5 (Full Length – Maths & Science – Set 1, Set 2, ...):** Ranked strictly out of **120 Merit Marks** (Language excluded).
  - **Part 6 (Full Length – Mathematics – Set 1, Set 2, ...):** Ranked strictly out of **120 Merit Marks** (Language excluded).
- Students attempting Set 1 of any Part are ranked ONLY against students who attempted that exact same Set 1. NEVER mix different sets or mix Part 5 (Maths & Science) with Part 6 (Mathematics).

B. Class-Wise, Category-Wise & Subject-Wise Ranking:
- Maintain separate rankings strictly by configured exam category, class level (e.g., Class 6–8, Class 9–10, Class 11–12 where supported), and subject/stream.
- Provide independent section-wise performance & ranking within Full Length sets (Part 5 & Part 6). Never combine unrelated subject ranks.

C. Language Paper – Strict Qualifying Rule in Rankings:
- Language (30 marks total: 8 English + 22 Hindi; Combined >= 9 = PASS, < 9 = FAIL) is strictly QUALIFYING ONLY.
- Language marks must NEVER increase or decrease Merit Score or Rank in Part 5, Part 6, or legacy 70-mark Language + Common Paper sets.
- Provide an Admin-configurable leaderboard policy for Language-failed (< 9/30) attempts in Part 5, Part 6, and legacy 70-mark sets:
  - Option 1: Display on leaderboard with a clear "Not Qualified (Language Failed)" badge without adding Language marks.
  - Option 2: Exclude Language-failed attempts from official Merit Rank while still displaying their Merit Score (e.g., X / 120 or X / 40) & "Language: FAIL (< 9/30)" on their personal Result Card.

D. Overall Merit Ranking, Percentile & Tie-Breaking:
- Calculate Overall Merit strictly from configured merit-bearing components only (excluding Language marks and excluding Reattempts).
- Support Admin-configurable tie-breaking rules (e.g., higher merit score -> higher accuracy / fewer negative marks -> less time taken, OR shared equal ranks when scores tie). Do NOT invent or hardcode unverified official tie-breaking rules.
- Calculate accurate Percentile alongside Rank (`((Total Participants - Rank) / Total Participants) * 100`, handling single-participant edge cases cleanly).

